# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Cached OSM / geo data (regenerable, large)
data/cache/*
!data/cache/.gitkeep
# ...except the footprints, which are tracked on purpose. A CI runner has no
# cache, and nothing in this repo can rebuild the parquet -- the Overpass fetch
# lives in height_coverage.py and the export script never calls it. Tracking it
# also pins the OSM snapshot, so a daily rebuild changes the tiles when the
# date changes and not when somebody edits a building in Astana.
!data/cache/astana_buildings.parquet
# Same reasoning for the trees, and it is a much smaller file.
!data/cache/astana_trees.parquet
# ...and the detected canopy, which the shadow model now reads.
!data/cache/astana_canopy.parquet
# ...and the street tables the API routes on. These are the graph reduced to
# what a request actually reads -- see backend/core/streets.py -- and they are
# tracked for a harder reason than the others: the graphml they come from is
# 65 MB and gitignored, so a deploy that did not carry these would have to
# rebuild it from Overpass before it could answer anything.
# The directory has to be re-included before anything inside it can be: git
# never looks inside a directory it has already excluded, so the file patterns
# below do nothing on their own.
!data/cache/streets/
!data/cache/streets/**
# ...and the canopy built from measured heights, which it reads in preference.
# Rebuilding it means 120 MB off S3 and several minutes of raster work, so a CI
# runner that had to do it nightly would be paying for an answer that changes
# only when Meta publish a new map -- which is to say, almost never.
!data/cache/astana_canopy_height.parquet
# ...and the named places behind the search index. Same reasoning again: the
# Overpass fetch lives in scripts/fetch_places.py and the index export never
# calls it, so a fresh checkout could not rebuild this.
!data/cache/astana_places.parquet
frontend/public/*.pmtiles
# ...except the basemap, for the reason the footprints are tracked: nothing in
# this repo can rebuild it. It is a Protomaps extract of the same bounding box
# the map clamps itself to -- 70.3688,50.7669,72.3875,51.4848 -- and it changes
# only when Protomaps publish a new build, which is to say never on our account.
# A deploy without it is a blank grey page.
#
#   pmtiles extract https://build.protomaps.com/<YYYYMMDD>.pmtiles my_area.pmtiles \
#     --bbox=70.3688,50.7669,72.3875,51.4848
!frontend/public/my_area.pmtiles

# Env & editors
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
# Precomputed shadow tiles (regenerable: scripts/export_shadow_tiles.py)
frontend/public/shadows/
